<Window xmlns="https://github.com/avaloniaui"
        xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
        xmlns:cards="using:TanMenu.Wpf.Views.Settings"
        x:Class="TanMenu.Wpf.Dialogs.AboutWindow"
        SizeToContent="WidthAndHeight"
        CanResize="False"
        ShowInTaskbar="False"
        WindowStartupLocation="CenterOwner"
        Background="{DynamicResource SurfaceBaseBrush}">

  <!--
    ══ THE ABOUT BOX ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
    Round 8, Task 4. 关于 was a TabItem of the Options dialog (and, before Round 5 item 2, a
    full-page overlay over 应用); it is a window of its own now, opened from the menu band's 关于
    item and by nothing else.

    WHY A WINDOW AND NOT A TAB. PUBLISHED, win-property-win: "Is the content solely an
    application's attributes? If so, use an About box." It is: this window's whole content is the
    product tile, the publisher, the version and the copyright, and not one of them is settable.
    PUBLISHED, cmd-menus, in the standard menu organisation: Help → About <program name>.
    Views/Settings/AboutCard.axaml already recorded the same fact from the other side — it was "the
    only group with no interactive control" on the surface it used to sit on.

    THE CONTENT IS THAT CARD, UNMOVED ON DISK, and it is hosted rather than copied. It keeps its
    ISettingsCard implementation and its ReloadFromConfig, which is what this window calls to fill
    it in (AboutWindow.axaml.cs); it writes nothing at all — since Round 8, Task 6 it does not even
    read the settings draft, only ConfigService for the UI language — so hosting it outside the
    settings surface commits nothing and discards nothing.

    ROUND 8, TASK 4 LEFT THE CARD'S GROUP BOX IN PLACE AND TASK 6 DELETED IT, exactly as this
    comment said it would. The cost while it stood was visible in Task 4's own capture: 关于 appeared
    TWICE on a window whose whole content is four lines — once as this window's Title and once as the
    box's header, both written from AppLanguage's "About". A box round the only group on a surface
    is what PUBLISHED, ctrl-group-boxes, tells you to indicate on the larger surface instead, and
    here that surface is a captioned window. SizeToContent absorbed the change, as predicted.

    THE MEASUREMENTS BELOW WERE RE-TAKEN TWICE, AND THE SECOND TIME IS WHY THIS SENTENCE IS HERE.
    Task 6 said it had re-derived them and left Task 4's paragraph untouched under that claim, so
    for one commit this file promised numbers it did not carry. They are re-derived here on the
    build that ships, after the review round put the settings surface's body FontSize back (see
    Views/Settings/AboutCard.axaml — deleting the group box also deleted the last thing on this
    window that set a FontSize, so its four lines drew at FluentTheme's inherited 14).

    SizeToContent="WidthAndHeight" — the opposite choice from Dialogs/OptionsWindow.axaml, and for a
    reason that does not apply here. That window pins Width/Height because a TABBED dialog that
    resized per tab would break PUBLISHED, win-property-win: "Don't assign effects to changing
    tabs." This window has one page and no tabs, so there is nothing for a size to change under, and
    a fixed number would be a measurement to maintain for no gain. MEASURED on this build, at 150 %
    scale, through the window's UIA BoundingRectangle (which for an Avalonia window is the CLIENT
    rectangle): 346 x 195 physical px = 230.67 x 130 DIP in Chinese, 346 x 193 = 230.67 x 128.67 in
    English — i.e. the HEIGHT really does move and this window really does follow it, while the
    width is pinned in both languages by the same line, the copyright, which is identical in both.
    (For anyone comparing captures, the two earlier states in Chinese: 377 x 279 with Task 4's group
    box in place, and 393 x 211 — 262 x 140.67 DIP, the figure Task 6's own report records in its
    §3.4 — with the box gone but the body still at 14. Neither of those builds' ENGLISH width was
    re-taken here and neither is claimed.) The outer
    window is 368 x 251 physical (245.33 x 167.33 DIP), read off PrintWindow's GetWindowRect: a
    22 x 56 physical px frame, the same frame Dialogs/OptionsWindow.axaml measured. Both are far
    inside the PUBLISHED floor, win-property-win's "Support the minimum Windows Vista screen
    resolution of 800 x 600 pixels".

    CanResize="False", ShowInTaskbar="False", no Icon — PUBLISHED, win-dialog-box: "Dialog boxes
    don't have title bar icons", "Resizable dialogs can have a Maximize button" (so a fixed one has
    none), "Don't disable the Close button." NONE OF THOSE COME OUT RIGHT FROM THE MARKUP ALONE, as
    Round 8, Task 2 measured on the Options dialog: Windows still draws a live Minimize box and
    still falls back to the OWNER's icon. Dialogs/DialogCaption.cs is that task's Win32 correction,
    moved out of OptionsWindow in this one so both dialogs share it, and this window's OnOpened
    calls it. Its remarks carry the measurement.

    THE TITLE IS 关于 / About, written by ApplyText() from AppLanguage's "About" key rather than
    declared here — the same key the card's own group head takes, so the window and its content can
    never disagree, and the same reason OptionsWindow writes its title from code: AppLanguage has no
    change notification.

    DISMISSAL: 确定, Enter, Esc and the title-bar ×, all closing the window and doing nothing else.
    There is nothing here to commit, so there is no Cancel to distinguish from an OK and no discard
    prompt to raise; IsDefault and IsCancel are both on the one button, which is what a one-button
    dialog does with the two keys. TWO OF THE FOUR WERE EXERCISED on this build — 确定 through UIA's
    InvokePattern and Esc through a posted WM_KEYDOWN — and both closed the window and re-enabled the
    launcher. Enter and the × were NOT: Enter needs the AccessKey/default-button path this machine
    has no keyboard for beyond posted messages, and the × needs a click. Neither is app code — they
    are IsDefault and the platform's own close — but neither is claimed as measured.
  -->
  <StackPanel Margin="11">

    <!-- The 关于 card exactly as the settings surface has it. x:Name so the code-behind can call
         ReloadFromConfig on it — nothing else reaches in. -->
    <cards:AboutCard x:Name="About" />

    <!-- NO TOP MARGIN, and that is arithmetic rather than an omission. PUBLISHED, vis-layout:
         "Between unrelated controls — 7 / 11", and the card above already carries exactly that 11 as
         its own bottom margin. WHERE THAT 11 LIVES CHANGED IN ROUND 8, TASK 6 and the arithmetic did
         not: it used to come from Themes/Shell/Launcher.axaml's
         HeaderedContentControl.tm-group-box (Margin="0,0,0,11", "two settings groups are as
         unrelated as two controls on one page get"); that rule and the box it styled are both
         deleted, and Views/Settings/AboutCard.axaml states the same 11 on its own root Grid so this
         row still has nothing to state. Stating a second 11 here would render 22.
         The row itself is right-aligned and the button is PUBLISHED at
         "Command buttons — 75x23"; 11 on every side of the window is the PUBLISHED dialog margin
         ("Dialog box margins — 7 DLU / 11 relative pixels on all sides"), on the StackPanel above.
         AboutWindowTests reads all of that back off this markup. -->
    <StackPanel x:Name="ButtonRow" Orientation="Horizontal" HorizontalAlignment="Right">
      <Button x:Name="OkBtn" Width="75" Height="23"
              IsDefault="True" IsCancel="True" Click="OnOkClick" />
    </StackPanel>

  </StackPanel>
</Window>
